  "worked_solution": "First, let's add a $Y=-2X-2$ row to our table.\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $2$ | $0$ | $-2$ | $-4$ | $-6$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, ${f}_{X}(x)={f}_{Y}(y)$ for corresponding values of $X$ and $Y.$ Therefore, the distribution of $Y$ is as follows:\n\n| $y$ | $2$ | $0$ | $-2$ | $-4$ | $-6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ |\n\nSo, we have $a=2,b=-2,c=0.3,$ and therefore $a+b+c=0.3.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
